<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · deity</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kura (god)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kura was the chief god of the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ebla">Ebla</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> in the 3rd millennium BCE. Known mainly from the Ebla archive, he appears as the protector of the king and the royal family, receiving offerings in the palace and in his own temple, and his consort was the goddess Barama. His cult seems to have been particular to Ebla and disappeared with the city.</p></div>
